WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:02.734
-Enjoy yourself.
Welcome, everybody.

00:00:02.734 --> 00:00:04.634
Welcome, welcome.
Welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:04.634 --> 00:00:06.601
You're here. You made it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:06.601 --> 00:00:08.934
Thank you for watching.

00:00:08.934 --> 00:00:10.534
Let's get to some news here.

00:00:10.534 --> 00:00:12.200
Well, guys,
today, President Biden

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:14.667
kicked off a three-week
travel blitz

00:00:14.667 --> 00:00:16.667
to highlight
his economic agenda called

00:00:16.667 --> 00:00:19.200
the Investing in America Tour.

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:22.000
Yep. You know all the excitement
for the Taylor Swift tour?

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:25.467
This isn't that. Yeah. Yeah.

00:00:25.467 --> 00:00:27.000
Yeah, when they heard,
Ticketmaster was like,

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:30.100
"We got plenty of seats
for this one."

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:32.934
Meanwhile, a new poll found
that nearly half of Democrats

00:00:32.934 --> 00:00:35.901
don't want
Biden to run again in 2024.

00:00:35.901 --> 00:00:39.901
Yeah. Half do and half don't.

00:00:39.901 --> 00:00:44.834
So I'm guessing they just polled
Joe Biden and Kamala Harris.

00:00:44.834 --> 00:00:47.501
"I do."
"I don't."

00:00:48.467 --> 00:00:50.267
But Biden's on tour
to promote his agenda,

00:00:50.267 --> 00:00:52.968
and at the same time,
Trump's on tour campaigning.

00:00:52.968 --> 00:00:54.167
Yeah, they're both on the move,

00:00:54.167 --> 00:00:55.567
but their tours
are actually very different.

00:00:55.567 --> 00:00:56.701
I'll show you what I mean.

00:00:56.701 --> 00:00:58.601
For instance, on Biden's tour,

00:00:58.601 --> 00:01:01.167
he's preparing to start his
re-election campaign.

00:01:01.167 --> 00:01:03.133
On Trump's tour,
he's preparing to start

00:01:03.133 --> 00:01:05.434
smuggling McRibs into prison.

00:01:05.434 --> 00:01:07.033
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Wow!

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:08.400
-You can't...

00:01:13.801 --> 00:01:16.400
"Throw it over the wall"!
-"No, throw it!"

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:18.767
-Next up on Biden's tour,
when he goes off script,

00:01:18.767 --> 00:01:20.834
his staff thinks, "OMG."

00:01:20.834 --> 00:01:22.300
On Trump's tour,
when he goes off script,

00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:24.834
his lawyers think, "FML."

00:01:24.834 --> 00:01:26.667
"Uh..."

00:01:28.167 --> 00:01:30.334
Next up, Trump wanders off
into topics

00:01:30.334 --> 00:01:34.234
he shouldn't discuss,
while Biden just wanders off.

00:01:34.234 --> 00:01:36.234
[ Laughter ]

00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:43.133
Alright, here's another.

00:01:43.133 --> 00:01:45.400
Biden shows up onstage
wearing aviators

00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:47.400
like he's in "Top Gun,"

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:50.501
while Trump shows up onstage
like he's "Cocaine Bear."

00:01:53.968 --> 00:01:57.567
Next up, Trump travels
with the MyPillow guy,

00:01:57.567 --> 00:01:58.868
while Biden travels
with his pill caddy.

00:01:58.868 --> 00:02:00.200
Oh.

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:03.801
And, finally, Biden thinks
his future is bright,

00:02:03.801 --> 00:02:06.701
while Trump knows
his future is stormy.

00:02:06.701 --> 00:02:08.834
[ Cheers and applause ]
There you go.

00:02:11.033 --> 00:02:15.100
Speaking --
Speaking of Trump, last night,

00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:16.567
for the first time
in six months,

00:02:16.567 --> 00:02:20.334
he appeared on Fox News for
an interview with Sean Hannity.

00:02:20.334 --> 00:02:21.634
Yeah, apparently,
Trump was there

00:02:21.634 --> 00:02:23.734
to promote his next indictment.

00:02:23.734 --> 00:02:24.868
[ As Trump ]
It's going to be huge.

00:02:24.868 --> 00:02:26.000
I don't know when
it's going to happen,

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:28.601
but maybe --
maybe the next week.

00:02:28.601 --> 00:02:30.767
I don't know.

00:02:30.767 --> 00:02:33.634
You're going to find out
after the break.

00:02:33.634 --> 00:02:34.868
[ Normal voice ]
Some business news.

00:02:34.868 --> 00:02:37.634
Amazon has a new feature
that will alert customers

00:02:37.634 --> 00:02:40.501
about products
that are frequently returned.

00:02:40.501 --> 00:02:42.801
Just to be clear,
frequently returned

00:02:42.801 --> 00:02:44.467
doesn't mean
that they're bad products.

00:02:44.467 --> 00:02:45.734
It just means that
they're bought by people

00:02:45.734 --> 00:02:49.033
who are frequently drunk.

00:02:49.033 --> 00:02:51.901
Did you ask you guys hear
about the big Kia recall?

00:02:51.901 --> 00:02:53.300
It's not good. Check this out.

00:02:53.300 --> 00:02:55.634
-The recall alert
involving half-a-million Hyundai

00:02:55.634 --> 00:02:56.968
and Kia vehicles.

00:02:56.968 --> 00:02:59.701
The company is recalling more
than 500,000 vehicles

00:02:59.701 --> 00:03:02.300
in the U.S. and urging owners
to park them

00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:04.400
outside because of a fire risk.

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:07.267
-Oh, man! I just bought a Kia.

00:03:07.267 --> 00:03:09.133
-Oh, sorry about that, Tariq.

00:03:09.133 --> 00:03:12.834
-It's okay. Thankfully,
I still have my trusty Tesla.

00:03:12.834 --> 00:03:16.067
-[ Breathes deeply ] Oh.

00:03:16.067 --> 00:03:19.534
-"Oh" what?
-Roll the clip.

00:03:19.534 --> 00:03:22.634
-Well, new tonight, a recall
alert for Tesla drivers.

00:03:22.634 --> 00:03:24.300
The electric-car company
is recalling

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:28.367
more than 3,000 vehicles
over loose-bolt concerns.

00:03:28.367 --> 00:03:29.968
-Loose bolts?!

00:03:29.968 --> 00:03:31.767
-Yeah, I'm sorry
about that, Tariq.

00:03:31.767 --> 00:03:34.033
-Man, I'm so tired
of all these recalls.

00:03:34.033 --> 00:03:35.501
Man, they give me a headache.

00:03:35.501 --> 00:03:37.300
They're the reason
I have a prescription

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:38.434
migraine medication.

00:03:38.434 --> 00:03:39.701
-A recall alert.

00:03:39.701 --> 00:03:42.334
Pfizer is recalling
more than 4 million packages

00:03:42.334 --> 00:03:44.934
of a prescription
migraine medication.

00:03:44.934 --> 00:03:47.133
-Oh, come on!

00:03:47.133 --> 00:03:48.634
-I'm very sorry, Tariq.
I really am.

00:03:48.634 --> 00:03:51.601
-At this point, I'm scared
to even leave my house.

00:03:51.601 --> 00:03:54.200
I'm just going to stay home
and hide under my

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:59.968
Sunbeam queen-side seated --
-sized heated blanket.

00:03:59.968 --> 00:04:03.334
-A brand of heated blankets
sold on Amazon

00:04:03.334 --> 00:04:05.133
under recall tonight.

00:04:05.133 --> 00:04:08.667
Sunbeam queen-side seated --
-sized heated blankets

00:04:08.667 --> 00:04:10.033
are being recalled.

00:04:10.033 --> 00:04:13.000
-You've got to be kidding me!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:15.501
-This is terrible luck.
This is terrible luck.

00:04:15.501 --> 00:04:17.467
-What do I even
have left at this point?

00:04:17.467 --> 00:04:19.767
The dog food in my pantry?

00:04:19.767 --> 00:04:23.434
-I-I didn't even know
that you were a dog owner.

00:04:23.434 --> 00:04:26.234
What kind of food
do you buy it?

00:04:26.234 --> 00:04:27.267
-Thanks for asking.

00:04:27.267 --> 00:04:30.467
Well, we usually buy
Purina Plo --

00:04:30.467 --> 00:04:33.534
Pro Plan Veterinary Diets food.

00:04:33.534 --> 00:04:35.801
-An important recall alert
for dog owners this morning.

00:04:35.801 --> 00:04:39.567
The recall specifically
covers Purina's Plo --

00:04:39.567 --> 00:04:42.467
Pro Plan Veterinary Diets food.

00:04:42.467 --> 00:04:45.000
-That's it. I give up.

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:46.901
-No, there's got to be something
that we can do

00:04:46.901 --> 00:04:48.567
to get your mind off
all this stuff.

00:04:48.567 --> 00:04:50.501
-Like what?
-Well, you know what?

00:04:50.501 --> 00:04:52.133
Why don't you come
to my place and hang out?

00:04:52.133 --> 00:04:53.667
I have a new YETI cooler.

00:04:53.667 --> 00:04:55.968
I mean, we all have a YETI,
and I doubt they're

00:04:55.968 --> 00:04:57.634
recooling -- recalling.

00:04:57.634 --> 00:04:58.934
-[ Chuckles ] Recooling.

00:04:58.934 --> 00:05:01.400
-They're not going to recall
some of the recoolers.

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:03.467
-And YETI. We all have a YETI.

00:05:03.467 --> 00:05:05.367
They're recooling -- recalling.

00:05:05.367 --> 00:05:06.501
-"Recooling."

00:05:06.501 --> 00:05:08.701
-They're going to recall
some of their recoolers.

00:05:08.701 --> 00:05:09.968
-Well, we tried.
Tariq Trotter, everybody.

00:05:09.968 --> 00:05:10.968
You'll have a better...

00:05:10.968 --> 00:05:13.701
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:05:19.467 --> 00:05:21.801
Best in the biz.

00:05:21.801 --> 00:05:23.667
Switching gears,
I read that researchers

00:05:23.667 --> 00:05:26.534
developed new smart leggings
that tell you when

00:05:26.534 --> 00:05:28.934
it's time to take a break
from working out.

00:05:28.934 --> 00:05:32.033
[ Laughter ]

00:05:32.033 --> 00:05:33.868
While your regular jeans
tell you when it's time

00:05:33.868 --> 00:05:35.901
to get back to the gym.

00:05:35.901 --> 00:05:37.400
Smart leggings.

00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:39.133
You know it's weird when you're
talking to your trainer like,

00:05:39.133 --> 00:05:41.601
"I think someone just
hacked my pants."

00:05:41.601 --> 00:05:42.667
Well, get this.

00:05:42.667 --> 00:05:44.767
After a viral TikTok
caused confusion,

00:05:44.767 --> 00:05:49.601
Fruit Roll-Ups is urging people
not to eat the plastic wrap.

00:05:49.601 --> 00:05:51.467
It's nuts.

00:05:51.467 --> 00:05:53.267
That's like if Popsicles
had to remind people

00:05:53.267 --> 00:05:54.467
not to eat the stick.

00:05:54.467 --> 00:05:55.934
It's like, "Yeah."

00:05:55.934 --> 00:05:57.234
And, finally, a new study says

00:05:57.234 --> 00:06:00.334
Botox injections can alter
your brain chemistry

00:06:00.334 --> 00:06:03.501
and impact how you interpret
other people's emotions.

00:06:03.501 --> 00:06:04.601
It's weird.

00:06:04.601 --> 00:06:05.767
Usually when you get Botox,

00:06:05.767 --> 00:06:08.434
people can't interpret
your emotions.

00:06:08.434 --> 00:06:09.467
We have a great show.

